{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U22", "U15", "U35"],
      "pins": ["U22.2", "U15.2", "U35.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "ESTOP_SINK1", "ESTOP_SINK_ALL"],
      "obs": "On the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet the data input (pin 2) of U22 (SN74LVC1G07) is wired straight to GND, while its active-low output-enable (pin 1) carries the ESTOP_SINK1 control signal. The downstream buffers U15 and U35 take their data inputs from U22's open-drain output, so the whole branch cascade is driven from a node that U22 can never pull low.",
      "exp": "The specification states these SN74LVC1G07 parts are 'wired as /OE-controlled sinks' feeding ESTOP_OUT. For a non-inverting open-drain buffer used as an /OE-controlled sink, the data input must be held HIGH (e.g. +3V3) so that asserting /OE (low) pulls the open-drain output low and sinks current. With the input tied to GND the output is permanently high-Z regardless of /OE, so the sink never asserts.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config': U22 pin 2 -> GND symbol; U22 pin 1 (/OB) -> ESTOP_SINK1; U22 pin 4 (Y) -> R61/D29 and U15 pin 2; U15 pin 1 -> ESTOP_SINK2; U35 pin 1 -> ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL; U35 pin 4 -> ESTOP_SINK_ALL."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks, feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ESTOP_SINK1 branch indicator (LED_RED D29) can never light and the buffer cascade into U15/U35 starts from an undefined/floating node, so the per-branch e-stop indicator lights added in the July-2024 changelog ('Expand E-stop circuit to provide indicator lights for each branch') do not operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the intended design in the e-stop sink cascade: U22's data input is tied to GND instead of held high, which defeats the /OE-controlled-sink wiring described in the spec and prevents the ESTOP_SINK1 branch indicator and its downstream cascade from ever sinking. Other spec-documented items (16 MHz crystals, SM712 TVS placement, LTC4412/P-MOS USB path, GLOBAL_EN switch, CAN LED buffers) match the drawing and are not reported."
}

